  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asian Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to implement the following: (1) to continue law enforcement activities using Elephant Patrol Units, (2) to enhance the forest departments capacity for monitoring domestic elephants and integrate this system with the existing HVWSs monitoring system, and (3) to upgrade the current patrol system to use Smart patrol protocols especially the integration of Management Information SysTems (MIST) and CITES Monitoring Illegal Killing of Elephants (MIKE) monitoring systems. Smart is a term used to refer to the full suite of ranger patrolling techniques used by the rangers of Huai Kha Khaeng Wildlife Sanctuary, Thailand, which will be applied in Burma. These techniques include the physical training, the high quality of ranger patrol equipment, the high geographic and temporal intensity of field patrols, the use of the MIST system for data management, and a willingness to respond to threats in a robust adaptive management approach.</narrative>
  </description>
